+    // holds `kernel` multiply-adds per plane; one task per plane would cost far
+    // more than the arithmetic, and under CPU contention the caller would wait
+    // in the join for descheduled workers. Each task covers at least
+    // `PARALLEL_THRESHOLD` multiply-adds, so small problems run inline.
